From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mi10-arch <mi10-arch@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:00:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: umi: send the brightness level high byte first

The panel takes DCS Set Display Brightness (0x51) as an 11-bit level
with the high byte first; the stock kernel marks both Mi 10 panels
"mi,mdss-dsi-bl-dcs-big-endian-type". The driver used
mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness(), which sends the low byte first,
so the panel saw (low << 8 | high): every level whose low byte is 8 or
more clamped to full brightness, and levels such as 1024 (50 %) came
out almost black.

Use mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness_large(), which sends the high
byte first.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-xiaomi-umi.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-xiaomi-umi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-xiaomi-umi.c
index f1ded5b29..0dd151414 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-xiaomi-umi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-xiaomi-umi.c
@@ -528,7 +528,13 @@ static int umi_panel_bl_update(struct backlight_device *bl)
 
 	level = clamp_t(u32, backlight_get_brightness(bl),
 			ctx->cfg.bl_min ?: 1, ctx->cfg.bl_max ?: 0x7ff);
-	return mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness(ctx->dsi, level);
+	/*
+	 * The panel IC takes the 11-bit level high byte first (the stock
+	 * kernel marks both Mi 10 panels "mi,mdss-dsi-bl-dcs-big-endian-type").
+	 * The plain helper sends the low byte first, so most levels clamp to
+	 * full brightness and levels such as 1024 come out almost black.
+	 */
+	return mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness_large(ctx->dsi, level);
 }
 
 static const struct backlight_ops umi_panel_bl_ops = {
@@ -578,7 +584,7 @@ static ssize_t umi_panel_kick_store(struct device *dev,
 	int level, ret;
 
 	level = backlight_get_brightness(ctx->bl);
-	ret = mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness(ctx->dsi, level);
+	ret = mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness_large(ctx->dsi, level);
 	dev_info(dev, "kick brightness %d -> %d\n", level, ret);
 
 	return count;
